## Summary

An `ARRAY` declared as a local variable of a `FUNCTION` or `FUNCTION_BLOCK` is accepted by `ironplcc check` but fails in codegen on the first access. Only `PROGRAM` variables and globals work.

```st
FUNCTION Probe : DINT
VAR
    a : ARRAY[1..2] OF DINT;
END_VAR
    a[1] := 5;
    Probe := a[1];
END_FUNCTION

PROGRAM main
VAR
    r : DINT;
END_VAR
    r := Probe();
END_PROGRAM
```

```
error[P9999]: Capability is not implemented (yet!)
  = ... file=codegen/src/compile_array.rs&line=169
```

The same program with `FUNCTION_BLOCK` in place of `FUNCTION` fails identically. This is not about any particular operation — a plain element write is enough.

## Cause

The local-variable pass in `compile_user_function` handles only two initializer kinds and drops everything else on the floor:

```rust
match &decl.initializer {
    InitialValueAssignmentKind::Simple(simple) => { /* ctx.var_types */ }
    InitialValueAssignmentKind::String(string_init) => { /* data region + ctx.string_vars */ }
    InitialValueAssignmentKind::Reference(ref_init) => { /* register_ref_to_array_metadata */ }
    _ => {}
}
```

